---
layout: layouts/base.njk
pagination:
  data: activeLangs
  size: 1
  alias: lang
pageSlug: "resources"
pageTitle: resources
---
{% set t = i18n[lang] %}
{#- The library, as its own switch. `resourcesLibrary` decides whether the
   real grid shows or the "coming soon" block does — separately from whether
   the Resources PAGE exists at all, which is `visible.pages.resources`.

   It no longer says "or not env.isProduction". That escape hatch meant the
   dev site could never show the unrevealed state, so there was no way to
   check what a visitor saw before launch. The dev column does that job now,
   and it defaults to revealed. #}
{% set resourcesRevealed = visible.sections.resourcesLibrary %}
<header class="page"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="cue rise">{{ t.resources.cue }}</div>
  <h1 class="page-h1 rise-2">{{ t.resources.h2_thin }} <b>{{ t.resources.h2_bold }}</b></h1>
</div></header>

<section><div class="wrap">
  {% if resourcesRevealed and resources.length %}
  {#- THE FOUR DOORS, which the data has always had and this page never used.
     src/_data/resources.js files every resource by the MOMENT somebody is in
     when they need it rather than by subject, and says why: a visitor with a
     dead mixer does not know which category their problem belongs to, they
     know what just happened. The page was printing `format` — guide, diagram
     — which is the one thing a person in that state does not care about.

     So the doors are the way in, in the visitor's own words, and format is a
     refinement underneath. Nothing here explains how to use it: four phrases
     and a search box are the instructions.

     HIDDEN WITHOUT JAVASCRIPT. The filtering is in the browser, so `lib-js`
     is set by main.js and the controls stay out of the document until it is.
     Otherwise a no-script visitor gets four dead buttons above a grid that
     never changes. The grid itself works with or without. -#}
  <div class="lib" id="lib">
    <div class="doors" role="group" aria-label="{{ t.resources.cue }}">
      {%- for d in ["crisis", "growth", "planning", "lookup"] %}
      <button type="button" class="door" data-door="{{ d }}" aria-pressed="false">
        <span class="door-label">{{ t.resources["door_" + d] }}</span>
        <span class="door-n" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      </button>
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>

    <div class="lib-bar">
      <label class="lib-search">
        <span class="vh">{{ t.resources.search_label }}</span>
        <svg class="lib-mag" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
          <circle cx="7" cy="7" r="4.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4"/>
          <path d="M10.4 10.4 L14 14" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round"/>
        </svg>
        <input type="search" id="libQ" autocomplete="off"
               placeholder="{{ t.resources.search_hint }}">
      </label>
      <div class="fmts" role="group" aria-label="{{ t.resources.link_label }}">
        {%- for f in ["guide", "diagram", "checklist", "glossary-entry", "video"] %}
        <button type="button" class="fmt" data-fmt="{{ f }}" aria-pressed="false">{{ t.resources["fmt_" + f] }}</button>
        {%- endfor %}
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="resource-grid" id="libGrid">
      {% for r in resources %}
      {%- set rtitle = r.title[lang] or r.title.en or r.title[r.langs[0]] %}
      {%- set rsum = r.description[lang] or r.description.en or "" %}
      {#- The corpus the search reads, built once here rather than scraped out
         of the rendered card: a card shows a summary in one language and the
         symptoms not at all, and somebody typing "no sound" should still find
         the resource that lists it. -#}
      <div class="resource-card" data-moment="{{ r.moment }}" data-format="{{ r.format }}"
           data-text="{{ (rtitle ~ ' ' ~ rsum ~ ' ' ~ (r.symptoms | join(' '))) | lower }}">
        {% if r.photo %}<div class="resource-photo"><img src="{{ r.photo }}" alt="{{ rtitle }}" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div>{% endif %}
        <h3><a href="/{{ lang }}/resources/{{ r.slug }}/">{{ rtitle }}</a></h3>
        <p class="resource-kind">{{ t.resources["fmt_" + r.format] or r.format }}</p>
        {% if rsum %}<p>{{ rsum | md | safe }}</p>{% endif %}
        {% if r.link %}<a class="btn ghost" href="{{ r.link }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{{ t.resources.link_label }}</a>{% endif %}
      </div>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>

    {#- Shown only when a filter empties the grid. The way out is a button,
       not an instruction telling somebody to clear their filters. -#}
    <p class="lib-none" id="libNone" hidden>
      <span>{{ t.resources.none_text }}</span>
      <button type="button" class="btn ghost" id="libClear">{{ t.resources.none_cta }}</button>
    </p>
  </div>
  {% else %}
  <div class="empty">
    <h3>{{ t.resources.empty_title }}</h3>
    <p>{{ t.resources.empty_text }}</p>
    <div class="workline"><i></i></div>
    <a class="btn ghost" href="/{{ lang }}/contact/">{{ t.resources.empty_cta }}</a>
  </div>
  {% endif %}
</div></section>
